  rules: [
    "1️⃣ SANALUVCHI (COUNTABLE) — SANASH MUMKIN\n\n📌 Mevalar:\n  apple, banana, orange, mango, lemon\n  I eat an apple every day.\n\n📌 Sabzavotlar:\n  tomato, potato, carrot, onion\n  There are three tomatoes.\n\n📌 Boshqa:\n  egg, sandwich, cookie, cake\n  I have two eggs for breakfast.\n\n📌 -S qo'shish:\n  apple → apples\n  banana → bananas\n  box → boxes (x + es)\n  tomato → tomatoes (o + es)",
    "2️⃣ SANALMAS (UNCOUNTABLE) — SANALMAYDI\n\n📌 Suv va ichimliklar:\n  water, milk, juice, tea, coffee\n  I drink water. (Suv ichaman)\n\n📌 Don va non:\n  rice, bread, sugar, salt, flour\n  I eat bread for breakfast.\n\n📌 Go'sht va baliq:\n  meat, chicken, fish\n  I like fish.\n\n📌 Yog' va boshqa:\n  butter, cheese, oil\n  I don't eat butter.\n\n🔴 SANALMASGA -S QO'SHILMAYDI:\n  ❌ waters, milks, rices, breads\n  ✅ some water, a glass of water",
    "3️⃣ 'SOME' VA 'ANY' QOIDALARI\n\n📌 SOME (ijobiy, taklif):\n  I have some apples. (Menda bir nechta olma bor)\n  There is some water. (Bir oz suv bor)\n  Would you like some tea? (Choy istaysizmi?)\n\n📌 ANY (savol, inkor):\n  Do you have any apples? (Olma bormi?)\n  I don't have any milk. (Sutim yo'q)\n  Is there any water? (Suv bormi?)\n\n🔴 'Some' = ijobiy/taklif savol\n  ✅ I have some money. ❌ I have any money.\n  ✅ Would you like some tea? (taklif)\n\n🔴 'Any' = savol yoki inkor\n  ✅ Do you have any time? (savol)\n  ✅ I don't have any time. (inkor)",
    "4️⃣ 'THERE IS / THERE ARE'\n\n📌 THERE IS (bitta, sanalmas):\n  There is an apple on the table. (Stolda olma bor)\n  There is some water in the glass. (Stakanda suv bor)\n\n📌 THERE ARE (ko'p, sanaluvchi):\n  There are three apples in the bag. (Sumkada 3 ta olma bor)\n  There are some cookies on the plate. (Patnisda pechenye bor)\n\n📌 So'rash:\n  Is there an apple? — Ha/Yo'q\n  Are there any apples? — Ha/Yo'q\n\n🔴 There is → Is there (savolda invertatsiya)\n  ✅ Is there a doctor? ❌ Is there are a doctor?",
    "5️⃣ 'I LIKE' / 'I DON'T LIKE'\n\n📌 I like + ot:\n  I like apples. (Men olmani yoqtiraman)\n  I like water. (Men suvni yoqtiraman)\n\n📌 I don't like + ot:\n  I don't like onions. (Men piyozni yoqtirmayman)\n\n📌 Do you like ... ?\n  Do you like coffee? — Siz kofemi yoqtirasizmi?\n  Yes, I do. / No, I don't.\n\n📌 3-shaxs (he/she):\n  He likes apples. (U olmani yoqtiradi)\n  She likes coffee. (U kofeni yoqtiradi)",
    "6️⃣ 'A GLASS OF' / 'A CUP OF' / 'A PIECE OF'\n\n📌 Suv/sut (sanalmas):\n  a glass of water (bir stakan suv)\n  a glass of milk (bir stakan sut)\n  a bottle of water (bir shisha suv)\n\n📌 Choy/kofe (sanalmas):\n  a cup of tea (bir piyola choy)\n  a cup of coffee (bir piyola kofe)\n\n📌 Non/pirog (sanalmas):\n  a piece of bread (bir bo'lak non)\n  a piece of cake (bir bo'lak tort)\n  a slice of pizza (bir bo'lak pitsa)\n\n🔴 'Of' ishlatiladi sanalmas uchun:\n  ✅ a glass of water ❌ a water",
    "7️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA XATOLAR\n\n• I eat a water ❌ (I drink water ✓)\n• I like apple, it is my favorite ❌ (I like apples, they are my favorite ✓)\n• There is three apples ❌ (There are three apples ✓)\n• I have many homeworks ❌ (I have much homework ✓ yoki I have a lot of homework ✓)\n• I don't have some money ❌ (I don't have any money ✓)",
  ],
